WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.850
Each run compares every
notice with the state.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.888
A new open notice gets a create.

3
00:00:04.888 --> 00:00:09.401
A changed one, with a different fingerprint
or a changed rule, gets an update.

4
00:00:09.401 --> 00:00:13.800
When the provider closes it, the task
gets a close that asks for the re-read.

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.441
And if an open notice simply disappears
from a provider the kit read this run,

6
00:00:18.441 --> 00:00:22.788
it's marked absent, and its task gets
an update asking for the same re-read.

7
00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:25.976
A provider that wasn't read
is never marked absent.

8
00:00:25.976 --> 00:00:28.013
Unchanged notices write nothing.

9
00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:31.518
And the whole run is a dry run:
nothing is sent unless the

10
00:00:31.518 --> 00:00:35.090
scheduled run is told to send
and the settings allow it.
